  "title": "A text feed joins the homepage",
  "summary": "April made more of Pollinations visible and easier to use, while model routing and request handling kept changing underneath.\n\nThe homepage gained a toggle between image and text feeds, with an editor for generated text. The image editor also began fetching its model options from the API.\n\nApps, bots, image tools, and interfaces joined the project list throughout the month. Featured browsing, GitHub stars, and clearer sorting made the growing catalog easier to explore.\n\nGemini, GPT-4.1, Llama 4 Scout, and Mistral changes reshaped the text lineup. Aliases, vision metadata, and catalog cleanup helped clients find the intended capabilities despite the routing changes.\n\nText caching began accounting for the full POST body, errors gained upstream details, and image generation gained more fallback routes. API examples and agent-readable endpoint descriptions also got attention.",
